@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1726 = private unnamed_addr constant [22 x i8] c"loop-iterator-mutation", align 1
@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1727 = private unnamed_addr constant [518 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for mutations to an iterable during a loop iteration.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen iterating over an iterable, mutating the iterable can lead to unexpected\0Abehavior, like skipping elements or infinite loops.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aitems = [1, 2, 3]\0A\0Afor item in items:\0A    print(item)\0A\0A    # Create an infinite loop by appending to the list.\0A    items.append(item)\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Mutable Sequence Types](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#typesseq-mutable)\0A", align 1
