@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1875 = private unnamed_addr constant [844 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for relative imports.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AAbsolute imports, or relative imports from siblings, are recommended by [PEP 8]:\0A\0A> Absolute imports are recommended, as they are usually more readable and tend to be better behaved...\0A> ```python\0A> import mypkg.sibling\0A> from mypkg import sibling\0A> from mypkg.sibling import example\0A> ```\0A> However, explicit relative imports are an acceptable alternative to absolute imports,\0A> especially when dealing with complex package layouts where using absolute imports would be\0A> unnecessarily verbose:\0A> ```python\0A> from . import sibling\0A> from .sibling import example\0A> ```\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Afrom .. import foo\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Afrom mypkg import foo\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-tidy-imports.ban-relative-imports`\0A\0A[PEP 8]: https://peps.python.org/pep-0008/#imports\0A", align 1
