@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.1924 = private unnamed_addr constant [664 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `printf`-style format strings that have mixed positional and\0Anamed placeholders.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APython does not support mixing positional and named placeholders in\0A`printf`-style format strings. The use of mixed placeholders will raise a\0A`TypeError` at runtime.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A\22%s, %(name)s\22 % (\22Hello\22, {\22name\22: \22World\22})\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A\22%s, %s\22 % (\22Hello\22, \22World\22)\0A```\0A\0AOr:\0A```python\0A\22%(greeting)s, %(name)s\22 % {\22greeting\22: \22Hello\22, \22name\22: \22World\22}\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `printf`-style String Formatting](https://docs.python.org/3/library/stdtypes.html#printf-style-string-formatting)\0A", align 1
