@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2006 = private unnamed_addr constant [562 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the inclusion of invalid objects in `__all__`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AIn Python, `__all__` should contain a sequence of strings that represent\0Athe names of all \22public\22 symbols exported by a module.\0A\0AAssigning anything other than a `tuple` or `list` of strings to `__all__`\0Ais invalid.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0A__all__ = [Foo, 1, None]\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0A__all__ = [\22Foo\22, \22Bar\22, \22Baz\22]\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: The `import` statement](https://docs.python.org/3/reference/simple_stmts.html#the-import-statement)\0A", align 1
