@anon.bcaf8a6642ef434db28a340da408f3d7.2018 = private unnamed_addr constant [357 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for the use of a classmethod being made without the decorator.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AWhen it comes to consistency and readability, it's preferred to use the decorator.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    def bar(cls): ...\0A\0A    bar = classmethod(bar)\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```python\0Aclass Foo:\0A    @classmethod\0A    def bar(cls): ...\0A```\0A", align 1
